---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Bow from "../components/Bow.astro";
import Waterline from "../components/Waterline.astro";
import IconLighter from "../components/IconLighter.astro";
import IconDrydock from "../components/IconDrydock.astro";
import { logbookEntries, formatDate } from "../lib/logbook";

const recent = (await logbookEntries()).slice(0, 3);
---
<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="headline">
        <h1 class="hull">Your machine has more in it than you think.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="above">
        <p class="sub">
          RAM is expensive right now, and high-end games keep asking for more of it. Salvage is open-source tools
          and engine fixes that get more out of the hardware you already have, starting with Unreal Engine. It's early: two tools are in the
          repository, and there's no release yet.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bow-cell">
        <Bow />
      </div>
      <div class="below">
        <p class="tagline hull">We don't sell you a new ship. We get yours sailing.</p>
        <p class="caption">Draft marks in gigabytes. A ship that carries less rides higher. (An illustration, not a measurement.)</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Waterline above="var(--deep-sea)" below="var(--ground)" shape="angle-reverse" stripe="var(--antifouling)" />

  <section class="why wrap">
    <h2 class="hull">Upgrading is the usual answer. Right now it's an expensive one.</h2>
    <div class="why-copy">
      <p>
        A machine gets written off when a game or an editor wants more memory than it has. We would rather find out
        how much of that memory the work really needs, and cut what it doesn't.
      </p>
      <p>
        A fix like that helps everyone. The old laptop gets a game that runs. The big workstation gets its memory
        back.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Waterline above="var(--ground)" below="var(--rescue-orange)" shape="angle" />
  <section class="punchout">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="hull">Somebody called your machine a wreck. <span>We'd like a look at it.</span></h2>
      <p>
        Laptops with 8 GB of memory. Desktops a few graphics cards behind. The Mac you were told isn't for game
        development. Those are the machines we're working for.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Waterline above="var(--rescue-orange)" below="var(--ground)" shape="angle-reverse" />

  <section class="streams wrap" aria-labelledby="streams-title">
    <h2 class="hull streams-title" id="streams-title">What we're working on</h2>

    <article class="stream">
      <IconLighter class="stream-icon" />
      <div>
        <h3 class="hull">Lighter Unreal</h3>
        <p class="lede">Make Unreal Engine games and the editor run on lower-powered machines, memory first.</p>
        <p>
          A lighter is a barge that takes cargo off a ship so it can float into shallow water. Same job here: take
          load off the engine so big games fit on small machines.
        </p>
        <p class="now">
          First tool: <a href="/charts/salvage-soundings/"><code>salvage soundings</code></a> reads a memory capture
          and shows where the memory goes, and whether the run fits 8, 12 and 16 GB machines.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="stream">
      <IconDrydock class="stream-icon" />
      <div>
        <h3 class="hull">Unreal on Mac</h3>
        <p class="lede">Make developing with Unreal Engine on macOS fast and pleasant.</p>
        <p>
          Plenty of people build games on a Mac. The editor, the builds and the tools around them should feel like
          they belong there, not like they're putting up with it.
        </p>
        <p class="now">
          First tool: <a href="/charts/salvage-doctor/"><code>salvage doctor</code></a> runs 12 checks on a Mac for
          the things that make Unreal slow or broken, and says how to fix each one.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <Waterline above="var(--ground)" below="var(--ground-2)" shape="angle" />

  <section class="built">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="hull built-title">How it's built</h2>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt class="hull">Tools ship here.</dt>
          <dd>Standalone tools live in the Salvage repository, under the MIT license.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="hull">Engine fixes go to Epic.</dt>
          <dd>
            Changes that belong inside Unreal Engine go upstream to Epic Games as pull requests, so they reach
            everyone who uses the engine, not only people who find this project.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="hull">No engine source here.</dt>
          <dd>
            Unreal Engine source stays under Epic's license. A check on every commit keeps it out of this
            repository.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Waterline above="var(--ground-2)" below="var(--ground)" shape="angle-reverse" />

  <section class="deck wrap">
    <div>
      <h2 class="hull">Two tools in the repo. No release yet.</h2>
      <p>
        <code>salvage doctor</code> and <code>salvage soundings</code> are in the repository, and you
        can <a href="/charts/salvage-doctor/#get-salvage">build them from source</a> today. There's nothing to download
        yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        Neither one saves memory by itself. Doctor finds what's wrong with a Mac's setup; soundings measures where a
        game's memory goes. They're how we'll find what to fix, and how we'll check the fixes. When a change does cut
        memory, it goes on the <a href="/manifest/">manifest</a> with its <a href="/soundings/">soundings</a>:
        before-and-after numbers on real machines.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="log">
      <h3>From the logbook</h3>
      <ol>
        {recent.map((e) => (
          <li>
            <time datetime={formatDate(e.data.date)}>{formatDate(e.data.date)}</time>
            <span>{e.data.title}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <a href="/logbook/">Read the whole logbook</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* ---- Hero ---- */
  .hero {
    --bow-w: min(40vw, 36rem);
    --below-h: calc(var(--bow-w) * 0.4615);
    background: var(--night-sea);
    color: var(--foam);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) var(--bow-w);
    grid-template-rows: auto 1fr var(--below-h);
    column-gap: var(--s-7);
    padding-top: var(--s-8);
  }
  .headline {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    grid-row: 1;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    padding-bottom: var(--s-5);
  }
  .above {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 2;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    padding-top: var(--s-4);
  }
  .bow-cell {
    grid-column: 2;
    grid-row: 2 / 4;
    align-self: end;
  }
  .below {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 3;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 1rem + 4.6vw, 5.5rem);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 24ch;
  }
  .sub {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--steel);
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin: var(--s-5) 0 0;
  }
  .tagline {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    font-weight: 800;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
  .caption {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--sea-glass);
    margin: var(--s-4) 0 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero {
      --bow-w: min(78vw, 26rem);
    }
    .hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      grid-template-rows: auto;
      padding-top: var(--s-7);
    }
    .headline,
    .above {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: auto;
    }
    .above {
      padding: 0 0 var(--s-6);
    }
    .bow-cell {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: auto;
      width: var(--bow-w);
      justify-self: end;
      margin-right: calc(var(--gutter) * -1);
    }
    .below {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: auto;
      background: var(--deep-sea);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 100vmax var(--deep-sea);
      clip-path: inset(0 -100vmax);
      padding-block: var(--s-6) var(--s-4);
    }
  }

  /* ---- Shared section bits ---- */
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ---- Why ---- */
  .why h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.2rem + 2.6vw, 3.5rem);
  }
  .why {
    padding-block: var(--s-8) var(--s-4);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    column-gap: var(--s-8);
  }
  .why-copy {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .why-copy p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .why-copy p + p {
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }

  /* ---- The punchout: Rescue Orange, used big once ---- */
  .punchout {
    background: var(--rescue-orange);
    color: var(--night-sea); /* 5.75:1 */
    padding-block: var(--s-6) var(--s-7);
  }
  .punchout h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-5);
    max-width: 21ch;
    line-height: 0.98;
  }
  .punchout h2 span {
    display: block;
  }
  .punchout p {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: var(--s-6) 0 0;
  }

  /* ---- Workstreams ---- */
  .streams {
    padding-block: var(--s-7) var(--s-5);
  }
  .streams-title,
  .built-title {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-5);
  }
  .stream {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--s-6);
    padding-block: var(--s-7);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--rule);
    max-width: 58rem;
  }
  .stream :global(.stream-icon) {
    width: 8rem;
    height: 8rem;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 10px 18px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.28));
    transition: transform 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1);
  }
  .stream:hover :global(.stream-icon) {
    transform: translateY(-4px) rotate(-4deg);
  }
  .stream h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .stream p {
    margin: var(--s-3) 0 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.45;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .now {
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: var(--s-4) !important;
  }
  .now a {
    color: var(--mark);
  }
  .now code,
  .deck code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.84em;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* ---- How it's built ---- */
  .built {
    background: var(--ground-2);
    padding-block: var(--s-6) var(--s-7);
  }
  dl {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 62rem;
  }
  dl > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
    gap: var(--s-6);
    padding-block: var(--s-5);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--rule);
  }
  dt {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 800;
  }
  dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
    padding-top: 0.3rem;
  }

  /* ---- Where things stand ---- */
  .deck {
    padding-block: var(--s-8) var(--s-8);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    gap: var(--s-8);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .deck h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
  }
  .deck p {
    margin: var(--s-4) 0 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .log h3 {
    font-stretch: var(--stretch-sign);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-weight: 750;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 var(--s-4);
  }
  .log ol {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-5);
    padding: 0;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--antifouling);
  }
  .log li {
    padding: 0 0 var(--s-4) var(--s-4);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }
  .log time {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .log span {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .why,
    .deck {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      row-gap: var(--s-5);
    }
    .stream {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--s-4);
    }
    .stream :global(.stream-icon) {
      width: 5.5rem;
      height: 5.5rem;
    }
    dl > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--s-2);
    }
  }
</style>
